<h1>About this site</h1>
    <p class="lead">gemini2k Tools is a collection of tools built one by one and published by a practitioner who has worked on information systems and data in the Korean public sector — tools that were actually needed on the job.</p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>IT audit, security reviews, de-identification of personal data and GIS analysis involve many small, repetitive tasks: tabulating audit findings, converting coordinate systems, masking files that contain personal data, comparing two CSV files. Installing software every time, or uploading work data to an unfamiliar website, is both tedious and risky.</p>
    <p>So the goal is <strong>tools that need no installation, never send your data anywhere, and finish right inside your browser</strong>.</p>

    <h2>Operating principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your input is not sent to a server.</strong> Almost every tool computes only inside your browser. Tools that call an external service, such as map tiles or coordinate lookups, say so on screen.</li>
      <li><strong>We show our sources.</strong> Tools that touch laws or standards (privacy, audit checklists, tax and insurance calculations, etc.) state which standard they follow and make clear that results are for reference.</li>
      <li><strong>We verify before publishing.</strong> Calculators are checked against known values (standard test vectors, official examples), and every page passes automated error checks before it is deployed.</li>
      <li><strong>Only commercially safe open source.</strong> External libraries are limited to permissive licenses such as MIT, Apache and BSD, and are hosted on this site itself to reduce third-party tracking.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Main tool areas</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="cat-audit.html">Audit &amp; verification</a> — findings registers, requirements traceability, checklists and other IT audit tools</li>
      <li><a href="cat-security.html">Security</a> · <a href="cat-pii.html">Privacy</a> — PII detection and masking, pseudonymization, re-identification risk checks, password and encryption tools</li>
